[
  {
    "runtag": "cfda-adarewriter-chiq-llm4cs-splade",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "8-2",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Actually, I wanted to know how someone gets started with tattooing as a hobby. Any idea what the basic steps are?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To get started with tattooing as a hobby, follow these basic steps:\n\n1. **Research and Learn**: Familiarize yourself with tattooing techniques, equipment, and hygiene practices. Watching tutorials and reading guides can be very helpful.\n\n2. **Gather Supplies**: Invest in essential equipment such as a tattoo machine, needles, ink, gloves, and cleaning supplies. You might also want to get practice skin or fake skin to hone your skills before tattooing on real skin.\n\n3. **Prepare Your Space**: Set up a clean, well-lit area to work in. Make sure the surface is sanitized to prevent infections.\n\n4. **Practice on Fake Skin**: Start by practicing your designs on fake skin or fruits like oranges or grapefruits, which mimic human skin texture.\n\n5. **Learn Basic Techniques**: Focus on mastering the basics such as outlining, shading, and coloring. These skills are fundamental to creating quality tattoos.\n\n6. **Follow Safety Protocols**: Always use clean needles and wear gloves. Clean the area to be tattooed and ensure proper sterilization of your tools.\n\n7. **Start Simple**: Begin with simple designs",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0007-71-06134:14": -0.2607824206352234
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I can draw well",
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! What specific equipment do you need to actually start tattooing? Like, tools and materials?",
          "user_rubrik": "What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To start tattooing, you'll need the following essential equipment and materials:\n\n1. **Tattoo Machine**: A reliable tattoo gun (either coil or rotary).\n2. **Tattoo Needles**: New, sterilized needles specific to your machine.\n3. **Tattoo Ink**: Professional-grade tattoo ink in the colors you want to use.\n4. **Power Supply**: A digital power supply to control the machine.\n5. **Foot Pedal**: For easy control of the tattoo machine.\n6. **Ink Cups**: Disposable cups to hold your ink during the tattooing process.\n7. **Gloves**: Disposable rubber gloves to maintain hygiene.\n8. **Cleaning Supplies**: Isopropyl alcohol, antibacterial soap, and disinfectants to clean your workspace and tools.\n9. **Practice Skin**: Fake skin or fruits (like oranges) to practice your technique before tattooing on real skin.\n10. **Aftercare Products**: Tattoo goo or ointments like A&D or Bacitracin for aftercare.\n\nAdditionally, consider investing in a starter kit that includes many of these items to make the process easier.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:15": 2.489649772644043,
            "clueweb22-en0007-71-06134:5": 1.2288401126861572,
            "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:15": 1.1262643337249756,
            "clueweb22-en0013-41-04803:0": 0.6791109442710876,
            "clueweb22-en0007-71-06134:4": 0.5521908402442932,
            "clueweb22-en0020-24-16033:20": 0.25057971477508545,
            "clueweb22-en0007-52-05511:3": 0.17189031839370728,
            "clueweb22-en0001-91-13299:7": 0.167077898979187,
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:14": 0.10592600703239441,
            "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:17": 0.06685981899499893,
            "clueweb22-en0014-92-17969:18": 0.056259945034980774,
            "clueweb22-en0007-71-06134:1": 0.0064194947481155396
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Cool, thanks! What about tattoo needles\u2014are there different types? What are they?",
          "user_rubrik": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, there are different types of tattoo needles, each designed for specific purposes. Here are the main categories:\n\n1. **Round Liner (RL)**: These needles are used for outlining designs. They create fine lines and are ideal for detailed work.\n\n2. **Round Shader (RS)**: These needles are used for shading and filling in areas. They allow for smoother transitions between colors.\n\n3. **Flat Needles**: These are used for creating shapes and intricate shading. They are effective for making sharp edges, like squares or stars.\n\n4. **Magnum Needles**: There are two types:\n   - **Round Magnum (RM)**: Best for coloring in larger areas without applying too much pressure, making them suitable for sensitive skin.\n   - **Stacked Magnum (M1)**: Great for blending and shading in smaller areas.\n\nEach type of needle has different sizes, which affects the thickness of the lines or the amount of ink deposited. Choosing the right needle is essential for achieving the desired effect in your tattoo work.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:5": 1.9380515813827515,
            "clueweb22-en0017-62-10056:2": 1.7285054922103882,
            "clueweb22-en0016-40-05463:0": 1.031480312347412,
            "clueweb22-en0015-21-00443:1": 1.0123281478881836,
            "clueweb22-en0031-20-16817:0": 0.8460049033164978,
            "clueweb22-en0022-58-06316:0": 0.5278036594390869,
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:3": 0.46785271167755127,
            "clueweb22-en0027-55-08441:0": 0.4087187647819519,
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:4": 0.3657185435295105,
            "clueweb22-en0009-13-08595:0": 0.2427976280450821,
            "clueweb22-en0034-44-03802:0": 0.18138325214385986
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense. Where do people usually buy tattoo needles, especially if you\u2019re just starting out? Are there reliable shops or do you have to order online?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where to buy tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You can buy tattoo needles from various sources, including both local shops and online retailers. Here are some options:\n\n1. **Local Tattoo Supply Shops**: Many cities have specialized tattoo supply stores where you can find a range of needles, inks, and other tattooing supplies. This is a great option if you want to see the products in person and get advice from knowledgeable staff.\n\n2. **Online Retailers**: Websites like Amazon offer a wide selection of tattoo needles and kits. You can find various brands and types of needles, often at competitive prices. Look for reputable sellers with positive reviews to ensure quality.\n\n3. **Tattoo Supply Websites**: There are dedicated online stores for tattoo supplies, such as Painful Pleasures, Tattoo Supply, and Kingpin Tattoo Supply. These sites usually have a broader selection and may offer bulk buying options.\n\n4. **eBay**: You can also find tattoo needles on eBay, often at discounted prices. Just be sure to check the seller's ratings and product descriptions carefully.\n\nWhen starting out, consider purchasing a beginner's tattoo kit that includes needles, as this can be a more cost-effective way to get everything you need.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0013-41-04803:0": 0.8987918496131897,
            "clueweb22-en0031-20-16817:0": 0.801658034324646,
            "clueweb22-en0022-58-06316:0": 0.4038453698158264,
            "clueweb22-en0027-86-19967:0": 0.2881503999233246,
            "clueweb22-en0009-13-08595:0": 0.24379101395606995,
            "clueweb22-en0021-73-10825:0": 0.035799358040094376
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting, thanks! I also heard about \u201cREACH compliant\u201d needles before. What does \u201cREACH compliant\u201d mean in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "\"REACH compliant\" refers to compliance with the EU's REACH regulation, which aims to ensure that chemicals used in products, including tattoo inks and needles, are safe for human health and the environment. This regulation restricts the use of certain hazardous substances that may cause health issues, such as skin irritations or long-term health risks. In the context of tattoo needles, being REACH compliant means that the needles are manufactured without these harmful substances, ensuring a safer experience for both tattoo artists and clients. As a result, some tattoo artists may need to adapt to using new inks and needles that meet these safety standards.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0016-40-05463:0": 0.6931504011154175,
            "clueweb22-en0031-20-16817:0": 0.5967555046081543,
            "clueweb22-en0022-58-06316:0": 0.2624812126159668,
            "clueweb22-en0009-13-08595:0": 0.1348281055688858
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful! I live in Germany, so I guess I should definitely look for REACH compliant stuff. Do you know what learning resources I could use about tattooing\u2014books, courses or anything?",
          "user_rubrik": "What learning resources are available about tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You can find a variety of learning resources for tattooing, especially in Germany. Here are some options to consider:\n\n1. **Books**: Look for books on tattoo techniques, hygiene, and art. Titles like \"The Tattoo Dictionary\" by Trent Aitken-Smith and \"Tattooing A to Z\" by Huck Spaulding are great for beginners.\n\n2. **Online Courses**: Websites like Udemy offer courses on tattooing basics and techniques. You might find courses specifically focused on safety and REACH compliance, which is important in Germany.\n\n3. **YouTube Tutorials**: There are many tattoo artists who share their techniques and tips on YouTube. Channels that focus on beginner techniques can be particularly helpful.\n\n4. **Local Workshops**: Check out local tattoo studios or community centers for workshops. Some tattoo artists offer classes for beginners, which can provide hands-on experience.\n\n5. **Tattoo Conventions**: Attend tattoo conventions where you can meet artists, attend seminars, and learn about the latest techniques and safety standards.\n\nThese resources should help you get started on your tattooing journey while ensuring you adhere to safety and compliance standards in Germany.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0017-15-04485:4": -2.430772304534912
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I live in Germany"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thank you for all the great information! If you have any more questions about tattooing or anything else, feel free to ask. Good luck on your tattoo journey\u2014farewell!",
          "user_rubrik": null,
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": null,
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
