          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To start tattooing as a hobby, there are several important steps and considerations:\n\n1. **Research and Learn**: Familiarize yourself with tattoo art styles and techniques. Study both traditional and digital art, as this will help you develop your design skills.\n\n2. **Practice on Fake Skin**: Begin by practicing on synthetic skin or fruits like apples and pears to simulate the feel of tattooing on human skin. This will help you refine your technique before working on actual skin.\n\n3. **Invest in Good Equipment**: If you're serious about learning, consider purchasing a quality tattoo machine or starter kit with sterile supplies. While this can be an investment, it\u2019s crucial for safety and quality. Remember, tattoo machines and supplies often cost about the same as getting a small tattoo professionally done.\n\n4. **Safety and Hygiene**: Always prioritize sterile conditions. Use new needles, clean your workspace thoroughly, and ensure you\u2019re not under the influence of alcohol or blood-thinning medications when tattooing.\n\n5. **Start Simple**: Choose simple designs for your first tattoos, such as outlines or small symbols. This will make it easier to build your confidence and skills.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0007-71-06134:1": 0.3551088869571686
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I can draw well",
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Which basic equipments are absolutely necessary for a beginner tattoo setup?",
          "user_rubrik": "What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To start tattooing as a beginner, you'll need the following essential equipment:\n\n1. **Tattoo Machine**: Choose either a coil or rotary machine. For beginners, a rotary machine is often recommended due to its ease of use.\n\n2. **Tattoo Needles**: Make sure to have a variety of sterile, disposable needles suitable for different styles (lining and shading).\n\n3. **Tattoo Ink**: Invest in quality tattoo inks that are specifically designed for skin application.\n\n4. **Power Supply**: A reliable power supply is crucial to operate your tattoo machine effectively.\n\n5. **Foot Pedal**: This allows you to control the power of the machine hands-free.\n\n6. **Tattoo Chair**: A comfortable chair is important for both you and your client during the tattooing process.\n\n7. **Cleaning Supplies**: Disinfectants, antibacterial soap, and disposable gloves are essential for maintaining a sterile workspace.\n\n8. **Practice Skin**: Use synthetic skin or fruits to practice your technique before working on real skin.\n\n9. **Aftercare Products**: Items like tattoo goo or ointments for aftercare are important for healing.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:15": 0.7419876456260681,
            "clueweb22-en0013-41-04803:0": 0.5539222955703735
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "There are several types of tattoo needles, each designed for specific purposes:\n\n1. **Round Liner (RL)**: Ideal for outlining designs, providing clean lines.\n2. **Round Shader (RS)**: Used for shading and coloring in between the outlines created by the RL needles.\n3. **Flat Needles**: Best for creating intricate shapes and shading, such as squares or stars.\n4. **Magnum Needles (M1 and RM)**: M1 (stacked magnum) needles are used for blending and shading in smaller areas, while RM (round magnum) needles can cover larger areas with less pressure, making them suitable for sensitive skin.\n5. **Turbo Needles**: These are designed for faster ink delivery and are often used for larger areas.\n\nEach type of needle has its own size variations, which also impact the effect and technique used in tattooing.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:5": 3.04876708984375,
            "clueweb22-en0017-62-10056:2": 2.4371824264526367,
