  {
    "runtag": "genaius-full-rewrite",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "8-2",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm curious about tattooing 101. How do people usually begin learning to tattoo as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Starting to learn tattooing as a hobby often begins with improving your artistic skills, such as drawing, sketching, or painting, as these are foundational to creating tattoo designs. Many beginners practice on synthetic skin or fruit like oranges to get a feel for the tattoo machine and techniques without working on real skin. It\u2019s also important to learn about hygiene, sterilization, and safety protocols to ensure a clean and safe process. Some people take beginner tattooing courses or apprenticeships to gain hands-on experience and guidance from professionals. Since you already have a sealion tattoo, you might find inspiration in your own design journey as you explore this art form.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:0": 21.114900588989258
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That's helpful! What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik": "What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To start tattooing, you'll need several essential pieces of equipment. A tattoo machine (or gun) is the primary tool, used for both lining and shading. You'll also need tattoo needles, ink, and ink cups to hold the pigment. A power supply with a foot pedal and clip cord is necessary to operate the machine. For design transfer, stencil transfer paper and a marking pen are helpful. Beginners often use synthetic practice skin to hone their skills before working on real skin. Hygiene is critical, so cleaning supplies like green soap, sterilization tools (e.g., autoclave or ultrasonic cleaner), and disposable gloves are must-haves. Many starter kits include these items, making it easier to get everything in one package. Since you already have a sealion tattoo, you might find inspiration in your own design as you practice and refine your technique.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:15": 22.858600616455078,
            "clueweb22-en0020-24-16033:20": 22.18120002746582
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Tattoo needles come in various types, each designed for specific purposes. The main categories include round liners (RL), round shaders (RS), and magnum shaders (M1). Round liners are used for creating fine lines and detailed work, while round shaders are ideal for shading and filling smaller areas. Magnum shaders, on the other hand, are used for shading larger areas and blending colors smoothly. Within these categories, needles also vary in size, which affects the thickness of the lines or the density of the shading. For example, a 3RL needle creates thinner lines compared to a 9RL. Beginners often experiment with different needle types to understand their effects and find what works best for their style. Since you have a sealion tattoo, you might find it interesting to explore how different needle types contribute to intricate designs like yours.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:4": 15.520400047302246
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Where can beginners buy tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where to buy tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Beginners can purchase tattoo needles from online platforms like Amazon or eBay, which offer a variety of complete tattoo kits that include needles, machines, and other essential supplies. Brands such as Wormhole and Dragonhawk are popular for starter kits that include multiple needle types. These kits often come with additional items like ink, power supplies, and practice skins, making them convenient for those new to tattooing. Alternatively, specialized tattoo supply stores also provide individual needles and kits tailored to specific needs. If you're inspired by your sealion tattoo, you might explore kits that allow for detailed work, as they often include fine liner needles for intricate designs.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0030-49-10071:3": 27.246299743652344
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I see. What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "REACH compliance in tattoo needles refers to adherence to the European Union's REACH regulation, which stands for Registration, Evaluation, Authorization, and Restriction of Chemicals. This regulation ensures that products, including tattoo needles, meet strict safety standards by limiting the presence of harmful substances. For tattoo needles, this means they are manufactured without hazardous chemicals that could pose risks to human health or the environment. Using REACH-compliant needles is particularly important for maintaining safety and hygiene in tattooing, as it minimizes the risk of allergic reactions or contamination during the process.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0027-53-14611:2": 14.746000289916992
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s good to know. What are good online courses or learning materials about tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik": "What learning resources are available about tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For beginners looking to learn tattooing online, platforms like Udemy and Domestika offer courses tailored to various skill levels. Udemy has a range of tattoo design and technique courses, often taught by experienced tattoo artists, and includes lifetime access to materials. Domestika also provides creative courses, such as custom tattoo design using tools like Procreate, which might be particularly useful for digital design enthusiasts. Additionally, YouTube can be a great free resource for tutorials on tattooing basics, machine setup, and hygiene practices. Since you have a sealion tattoo, you might enjoy courses that focus on creating intricate and meaningful designs, drawing inspiration from your own tattoo journey.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0023-65-17245:9": 21.435699462890625
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
