  {
    "runtag": "genaius-summary-rewrite",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "8-2",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Hi! I\u2019m actually looking for info on tattooing 101. Like, how does someone even start doing tattoos as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Getting started with tattooing as a hobby involves a mix of learning, practice, and acquiring the right tools. First, research the basics of tattooing, including hygiene practices, skin anatomy, and the use of tattoo machines. Many beginners start by practicing on synthetic skin or fruit like oranges to get a feel for the equipment and techniques. You\u2019ll also need to invest in a beginner tattoo kit, which typically includes a tattoo machine, needles, ink, and sterilization supplies. Online tutorials and beginner tattooing courses can be a great resource to guide you through the process. Remember, tattooing on actual skin requires a deep understanding of safety and sterilization to prevent infections. If you\u2019re serious about pursuing this, consider apprenticing under a professional tattoo artist to gain hands-on experience and learn industry standards. Let me know if you\u2019d like more specific guidance or resources!",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0014-36-11223:0": 20.11840057373047
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik": "What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To start tattooing, you\u2019ll need several essential pieces of equipment. These include a tattoo machine (or gun) for both lining and shading, tattoo needles, ink, a power supply, and clip cords. Additionally, you\u2019ll require sterilization tools like an autoclave or ultrasonic cleaner to ensure hygiene. Other necessary items include disposable gloves, ink cups, tattoo grips, and practice materials such as synthetic skin. For beginners, a complete tattoo kit can be a convenient option as it typically includes all these essentials. Practicing on synthetic skin before working on real skin is highly recommended to build confidence and skill.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:15": 24.3794002532959,
            "clueweb22-en0020-24-16033:20": 22.963899612426758,
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:0": 19.836700439453125
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Tattoo needles come in various types, each designed for specific purposes in tattooing. The main categories include:\n\n1. **Round Liners (RL)**: These needles are tightly grouped in a circular pattern and are used for creating fine lines and detailed work.\n\n2. **Round Shaders (RS)**: Similar to round liners but spaced slightly apart, these are used for shading and coloring smaller areas.\n\n3. **Magnum Shaders (M1, M2)**: These needles are arranged in a straight line or stacked, making them ideal for shading and coloring larger areas.\n\n4. **Flat Needles (F)**: These needles are aligned in a single row and are often used for geometric designs and shading.\n\n5. **Single Needles**: These are used for extremely fine details and intricate line work.\n\nEach type of needle is available in different sizes, allowing for versatility in creating various effects. For beginners, it\u2019s essential to practice with different needle types on synthetic skin to understand their unique applications and build confidence.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0008-01-12699:6": 22.480499267578125,
            "clueweb22-en0008-01-12699:8": 21.94580078125
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Where can I buy tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where to buy tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You can purchase tattoo needles from various online retailers like Amazon, which offers a wide range of options for beginners and professionals. For example, brands like Wormhole and Dragonhawk provide kits that include assorted needles, often bundled with other tattooing supplies. These are available with fast shipping options, making it convenient to get started. Additionally, specialized tattoo supply stores online or in your local area are great places to find high-quality needles. Ensure that the needles are sterilized and compatible with your tattoo machine.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0011-42-12453:3": 23.422399520874023,
            "clueweb22-en0030-49-10071:3": 22.501800537109375,
            "clueweb22-en0007-61-11325:0": 20.56679916381836
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "REACH compliance in tattoo needles refers to adherence to the European Union's Registration, Evaluation, Authorization, and Restriction of Chemicals (REACH) regulation. This legislation ensures that chemicals used in products, including tattoo needles and inks, are safe for human health and the environment. For tattoo needles, REACH compliance typically involves ensuring that the materials used in their production do not contain harmful substances above permissible levels. This is particularly important in the EU, where strict standards are in place to regulate products that come into direct contact with the skin. If you\u2019re purchasing tattoo needles in Germany or elsewhere in the EU, look for products labeled as REACH compliant to ensure they meet these safety standards.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0029-03-12586:6": 17.798200607299805,
            "clueweb22-en0041-85-19451:0": 17.077299118041992
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I live in Germany."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Can you recommend any online tattoo courses?",
          "user_rubrik": "What learning resources are available about tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For online tattoo courses, platforms like Udemy, Skillshare, and Tattooing 101 offer beginner-friendly options. These courses often cover essential topics such as tattooing techniques, hygiene practices, and equipment handling. Additionally, some courses provide video tutorials and feedback from experienced tattoo artists, which can be valuable as you start practicing. Let me know if you'd like help finding a specific course that aligns with your goals!",
          "citations": {
