        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s really helpful, thanks! I can draw pretty well and have a bunch of sealion sketches\u2014maybe I\u2019ll start with those. What are some common mistakes beginners make in tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik": "What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "As a beginner, it's crucial to practice your designs on fake skin or fruit (like apples or pears) before tattooing real skin, since tattooing is permanent and requires skill development first [clueweb22-en0042-99-10026]. Always read the instruction manual for your equipment and watch teaching videos to understand proper setup and technique. Hygiene and safety are essential\u2014never tattoo without proper sterilization and cleanliness. Avoid impulsive decisions about designs, size, and placement; take time to reflect on what you want to create, as impulsive or poorly planned tattoos are often regretted later [clueweb22-en0014-18-08868]. Also, avoid tattooing under the influence and don't rush to do too many tattoos at once, as this can clutter your work and reduce its artistic impact [clueweb22-en0014-18-08868]. Would you like tips on safe tattoo hygiene practices?",
