          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s perfect. I like that there are vegan and safe choices! By the way, how much practice do most beginners need before tattooing someone?",
          "user_rubrik": "What learning resources are available about tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "It's recommended that beginners spend extensive time practicing on fake skin, fruit (like apples or pears), or even pig skin to simulate the challenges of tattooing on real skin. This practice helps you develop control and confidence with the tattoo machine. Many artists suggest practicing for several months, accumulating hundreds of hours, before attempting to tattoo a person. In professional settings, apprenticeships typically last 1\u20132 years, during which you gradually progress from drawing to tattooing on practice materials, and finally to small tattoos on friends or volunteers under supervision. This long practice period ensures you have the necessary skills and hygiene knowledge to tattoo safely and effectively [clueweb22-en0016-15-15694][clueweb22-en0024-21-00136][clueweb22-en0042-99-10026][clueweb22-en0019-23-08097]. Are you interested in tips for practicing specific tattoo styles?",
