            "I have a sealion tattoo on my left shoulder."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That's okay for now! What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Tattoo needles are categorized based on their grouping and intended use. The most common types are: Round Liner (RL) needles, which are tightly grouped in a circle and used for creating crisp outlines; Round Shader (RS) needles, which are also circular but spaced further apart for shading and coloring small areas; Magnum (M1/M2) needles, which are arranged in a straight or stacked line and are ideal for shading and coloring larger areas; Flat needles, which are lined up in a straight row and are often used for making straight lines or geometric shapes; and Shader needles, which are designed specifically for blending and shading work. Needle size and configuration also matter\u2014smaller needles are used for fine lines and details, while larger groupings are better for shading and filling [DOC-1][DOC-7][DOC-6]. Would you like a visual guide to tattoo needle types?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:5": 0.07799281762728466,
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:4": 0.05876906801968991,
            "clueweb22-en0015-21-00443:7": 0.05703601489375268,
            "clueweb22-en0008-01-12699:6": 0.056604554865424435
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
