          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Hi! I was wondering, how do people usually get started with tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "To get started with tattooing as a hobby, many people first focus on developing their drawing and art skills, often by taking art classes or practicing at home. Beginner tattoo kits are widely available and typically include everything needed to start, such as a tattoo machine, sterilized needles, ink, and a teaching manual, making them suitable for hobbyists [DOC-1]. Online courses and tutorials can provide foundational knowledge, with options ranging from basic guides to more advanced techniques [DOC-3]. However, the traditional and most respected way to learn is through a tattoo apprenticeship, where you work under a professional artist to gain hands-on experience and learn about safety and hygiene practices, which are crucial in tattooing [DOC-4]. While online resources are helpful, hands-on training is essential for mastering the craft and ensuring safe practices. Are there any local tattoo apprenticeship opportunities?",
