      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that's more helpful! I'm in Germany\u2014can you tell me if there are requirements or regulations to start tattooing as a hobby here?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To start tattooing in Germany, you must register yourself and your premises with your local council, even if you are only tattooing as a hobby or from home. Tattooing without this registration is illegal and can lead to fines up to \u20ac20,000 or even jail time [DOC-1]. Local councils regulate tattoo parlors and home-based tattooing, and environmental health teams conduct inspections to ensure compliance with hygiene and safety standards [DOC-1]. You are also expected to follow strict hygiene protocols, such as using sterilized equipment, single-use needles, and medical gloves, to prevent the spread of diseases like hepatitis or HIV [DOC-1][DOC-5]. While there is no national licensing system, local authorities may require you to complete recognized training or an apprenticeship, and you may need to be vaccinated against hepatitis B [DOC-2]. Always check with your local council for specific requirements in your area. Do you want tips on building a tattoo portfolio or finding a mentor?",
