      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s more useful! About sterilizing tattoo equipment\u2014do you have instructions? Also, what counts as \u201csterilized\u201d exactly?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Sterilized tattoo equipment means all tools are free from any harmful bacteria or viruses, which is crucial for preventing infections. The gold standard is using an autoclave, which uses steam, heat, and pressure to eliminate pathogens in about 20 minutes, but these can be expensive [DOC-4]. For home hobbyists, a dry heat sterilizer (similar to a baking oven) is a more affordable option: place your metal tools in the device and heat them to the recommended temperature to kill bacteria [DOC-1][DOC-2]. Always use single-use, pre-sterilized needles and tubes when possible, and wear single-use gloves. Clean the skin with antiseptic before tattooing, and maintain personal hygiene by washing hands thoroughly and wearing a clean apron [DOC-3]. Keep in mind that in Germany, professional tattooists are required to follow strict hygiene standards, so even as a hobbyist, you should aim to match these practices for safety. Are there specific hygiene regulations for home tattooing in Germany?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:11": 0.07655363925933498,
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:10": 0.07155376401841973,
            "clueweb22-en0012-10-16285:7": 0.07071472234295192,
