      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "No links needed right now, thanks! Can you tell me more about the different types of tattoo needles? Like what shapes and groupings exist?",
          "user_rubrik": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Tattoo needles are grouped and shaped for specific tasks. Round liner (RL) needles are tightly grouped in a circle and are best for crisp outlines. Round shader (RS) needles are also circular but spaced further apart, making them ideal for shading or coloring between outlines. Magnum needles come in two main types: stacked magnums (M1), which are arranged in two rows for blending and shading smaller areas, and round magnums (RM), which are curved to cover larger areas gently\u2014great for sensitive skin or large color fills. Flat needles are arranged in a straight line and are used for bold lines, intricate shading, or geometric patterns. Needle size also matters: smaller groupings are used for fine details and outlines, while larger groupings are better for shading and filling [clueweb22-en0017-62-10056][clueweb22-en0022-31-15676][clueweb22-en0015-21-00443]. Would you like tips on choosing needle sizes for specific designs?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0017-62-10056:2": 0.07969243265548132,
            "clueweb22-en0022-31-15676:5": 0.07380205538100275,
            "clueweb22-en0015-21-00443:1": 0.07307793460156045,
