      {
        "turn": 10,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yes, tips on cleaning and safely disposing of used needles would be great! Also, can I get these needles at regular art supply stores?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where to buy tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To clean reusable tattoo tools, professional studios use an autoclave to sterilize equipment, ensuring all bacteria and viruses are eliminated. For home hobbyists, it's safest to use only pre-sterilized, single-use needles and dispose of them in a sharps or biohazard container\u2014never in household waste\u2014to prevent injury and contamination [clueweb22-en0046-30-10934:8]. In Germany, these containers can be purchased at pharmacies or online, and full containers should be returned to a pharmacy or a designated disposal site. Regular art supply stores generally do not carry tattoo needles, as these are specialized items subject to health regulations; instead, purchase from reputable tattoo supply shops or online retailers that offer pre-sterilized, individually packaged needles [clueweb22-en0015-21-00443][clueweb22-en0012-92-18666]. Are you interested in learning about aftercare for practice tattoos?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0046-30-10934:7": 0.052204068333100595,
            "clueweb22-en0046-30-10934:8": 0.05022483094772252,
            "clueweb22-en0015-21-00443:0": 0.037993687020598556,
            "clueweb22-en0012-92-18666:1": 0.037142299605947296
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I live in Germany.",
            "I am looking into how to start tattooing as a hobby."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 11,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yes, aftercare tips for practice tattoos would help a lot! Oh, and what does \u201cREACH compliant\u201d mean when it comes to tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Aftercare for practice tattoos on synthetic skin is simple: gently wash the practice skin with mild soap and water to remove excess ink, let it air dry, and store it in a clean, dust-free environment to prevent staining or damage. Unlike real skin, synthetic skin doesn't require ointments or bandaging, but keeping it clean helps you evaluate your work and reuse the surface for further practice. As for 'REACH compliant,' this refers to the EU's Registration, Evaluation, Authorization, and Restriction of Chemicals regulation, which sets strict limits on hazardous substances in tattoo products, including inks and needles. REACH compliance ensures that tattoo equipment sold in Germany and the EU is free from chemicals linked to allergies, genetic mutations, or cancer, making them safer for both artists and clients. Always look for REACH-compliant labeling when purchasing tattoo supplies in Germany to ensure legal and safe practice [clueweb22-en0000-83-16967][clueweb22-en0007-89-03397][clueweb22-en0000-53-19806].",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0000-83-16967:1": 0.032266458495966696,
