      {
        "turn": 11,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yes, aftercare tips for practice tattoos would help a lot! Oh, and what does \u201cREACH compliant\u201d mean when it comes to tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Aftercare for practice tattoos on synthetic skin is simple: gently wash the practice skin with mild soap and water to remove excess ink, let it air dry, and store it in a clean, dust-free environment to prevent staining or damage. Unlike real skin, synthetic skin doesn't require ointments or bandaging, but keeping it clean helps you evaluate your work and reuse the surface for further practice. As for 'REACH compliant,' this refers to the EU's Registration, Evaluation, Authorization, and Restriction of Chemicals regulation, which sets strict limits on hazardous substances in tattoo products, including inks and needles. REACH compliance ensures that tattoo equipment sold in Germany and the EU is free from chemicals linked to allergies, genetic mutations, or cancer, making them safer for both artists and clients. Always look for REACH-compliant labeling when purchasing tattoo supplies in Germany to ensure legal and safe practice [clueweb22-en0000-83-16967][clueweb22-en0007-89-03397][clueweb22-en0000-53-19806].",
