          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "equipment. What safety measures are crucial in tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik": "What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The most crucial safety measures in tattooing\u2014especially for a beginner with strong drawing skills\u2014are all about infection control and preventing cross-contamination. Here\u2019s what you must prioritize:\n\n**1. Sterilization & Equipment**\n- Always use single-use, sterile needles and disposable ink caps for each session.\n- Sterilize all reusable equipment with an autoclave; never reuse anything that penetrates skin.\n- Clean non-autoclavable surfaces (machines, countertops) with approved disinfectants.\n\n**2. Personal Hygiene**\n- Wash hands thoroughly before and after any procedure.\n- Wear new, disposable gloves for every client and change them if you touch anything non-sterile.\n\n**3. Workspace Setup**\n- Cover any surfaces or equipment that may be touched during tattooing with barrier film or plastic wrap.\n- Use biohazard and sharps containers for disposal of needles and contaminated materials.\n\n**4. Ink Safety**\n- Only use inks specifically made for tattooing; never dilute with non-sterile water.\n- Use fresh ink for each client.\n\n**5. Legal & Ethical**",
