      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "cartridges seem convenient. What are some essential supplies I should always have on hand while tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where to buy tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "To tattoo safely and effectively, always have these essential supplies on hand:\n\n**1. Hygiene & Safety**\n- Disposable gloves (change frequently)\n- Single-use, sterile cartridge needles (RL, RS, M1/M2 for different styles)\n- Barrier film/plastic wrap for covering surfaces and equipment\n- Biohazard and sharps containers for safe disposal\n- Medical-grade disinfectant for cleaning all non-disposable surfaces\n\n**2. Tattooing Equipment**\n- Rotary pen-style tattoo machine (Dragonhawk, Wormhole, Solong\u2014compatible with universal cartridges)\n- Power supply, foot pedal, clip cord\n- Practice skins and/or fruit (apples are great for you!)\n\n**3. Tattoo Process Supplies**\n- Tattoo ink (only professional, sterile brands)\n- Ink caps (single-use)\n- Transfer/stencil paper\n- Bandages and aftercare ointment\n\n**4. Maintenance & Setup**\n- Cleaning brushes for machine parts\n- Rubber bands, grommets, O-rings (for machine maintenance)\n- Practice skin for ongoing skill-building\n\n**Why this fits you:**",
