      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm curious about starting tattooing as a hobby. What are the first steps?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Since you already have strong drawing skills and a personal connection to tattoos, here\u2019s how to start tattooing as a hobby\u2014focused on safety, skill-building, and practical steps:\n\n**1. Build Tattoo-Specific Skills**\n- Even great artists need to adapt their drawing to tattooing. Practice your designs on paper, then move to practice skins (synthetic or fruit like apples/pears) before ever touching human skin. This is essential because tattooing is permanent and the technique is very different from drawing or painting.\n\n**2. Get the Right Equipment**\n- Invest in a reputable beginner tattoo kit. Look for kits that include:\n  - A reliable tattoo machine (gun or pen)\n  - Sterile needles\n  - Practice skin\n  - Power supply, foot pedal, and cleaning tools\n  - Basic inks (start with a few, focus on quality)\n- Recommended beginner kits: Solong, Dragonhawk, Yuelong, Wormhole, Stigma.\n\n**3. Prioritize Safety and Hygiene**\n- Learn proper sterilization: Use autoclaves or ultrasonic cleaners for",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0042-99-10026:8": -0.031169116497039795,
            "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:0": -0.04248145967721939,
