      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "fruit sounds fun! How do I choose the right tattoo machine for beginners?",
          "user_rubrik": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For a beginner in Germany with strong drawing skills, the best tattoo machine is a **rotary pen-style kit**\u2014specifically, the Dragonhawk, Wormhole, or Solong starter kits. These are consistently top-rated for ease of use, reliability, and value.\n\n**Why rotary pen kits?**\n- **User-friendly:** Pen shape feels natural for artists used to drawing, making the transition smoother.\n- **Quiet & low vibration:** Less intimidating and easier to control for precise linework\u2014ideal for practicing on apples or synthetic skin.\n- **Complete kits:** Include machine, power supply, needles, inks, and practice skin\u2014no need to buy extras separately.\n\n**Top beginner kits (all under \u20ac120):**\n- **Dragonhawk Atom/Pro Pen Kit:** Highly rated for smooth operation, durability, and beginner-friendly setup.\n- **Wormhole Tattoo Pen Kit:** Affordable, reliable, and comes with plenty of practice supplies.\n- **Solong Tattoo Pen Kit:** Good quality, easy to assemble, and includes wireless options.\n\n**What to look for:**\n- **Quality",
