      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "and compatibility. Do I need specific types of needles for different tattoo styles?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where to buy tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Yes, you need specific needle types for different tattoo styles. Here\u2019s what matters most for a beginner with strong drawing skills:\n\n**Needle Types & Their Uses**\n- **Round Liner (RL):** Tightly grouped, perfect for crisp outlines and fine lines. Essential for linework and detail.\n- **Round Shader (RS):** Looser round grouping, used for shading small areas and thicker lines.\n- **Magnum (M1, M2):** Flat or stacked needles, ideal for shading and color packing over larger areas.\n- **Flat (F):** Straight line, good for geometric work and some shading.\n\n**Compatibility**\n- Most beginner rotary pen kits (Dragonhawk, Wormhole, Solong) use universal cartridge needles\u2014easy to swap, safe, and compatible with most pen-style machines.\n- Kits often include a mix of RL, RS, and M1/M2 cartridges, covering all basic styles.\n\n**Why this fits you:**  \nWith your drawing skills, start with RL for outlines and M1/M2 for shading on practice skins or fruit. Universal",
          "citations": {
