      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, that makes sense! How do I ensure proper aftercare for tattoos?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where to buy tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "To ensure proper tattoo aftercare\u2014crucial for both healing and preserving your art\u2014follow this streamlined, evidence-based routine:\n\n**1. Immediate Care**\n- Keep the tattoo covered with a sterile bandage/wrap for the time your artist recommends (usually a few hours).\n- Wash hands before touching the tattoo.\n\n**2. Cleaning**\n- Gently wash the tattoo 2x daily with lukewarm water and fragrance-free, antibacterial soap.\n- Pat dry with a clean paper towel; never rub.\n\n**3. Moisturizing**\n- Apply a thin layer of a reputable, fragrance-free tattoo aftercare lotion (e.g., After Inked, Hustle Butter, or a vegan balm) after each wash. Too much lotion can suffocate the skin\u2014dab off excess.\n- Let the tattoo air dry before moisturizing to prevent \u201cbubbling\u201d or scab issues.\n\n**4. Protection**\n- Avoid soaking (baths, swimming) and sweating heavily for at least 2\u20134 weeks.\n- Keep the tattoo out of direct sunlight until fully healed; use sunscreen (",
