        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "once healed) to protect the colors. How long does it usually take for a tattoo to heal completely?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "A tattoo typically takes **2\u20134 weeks** for the surface skin to heal, but **full healing (including deeper layers)** can take up to **6\u20138 weeks**. Here\u2019s what you need to know:\n\n- **Surface Healing (2\u20134 weeks):** The tattoo will peel, flake, and may look dull or dry. This is normal\u2014don\u2019t pick at it. Keep it clean and moisturized with a fragrance-free, tattoo-specific lotion (like After Inked or Hustle Butter).\n- **Deeper Healing (up to 2 months):** Even after the skin looks healed, the tissue beneath is still repairing. Avoid heavy sun exposure and soaking (baths, swimming) until this phase is complete.\n- **Factors Affecting Healing:** Size, placement, your skin type, and how well you follow aftercare all matter. Good sleep, hydration, and nutrition speed recovery.\n\n**Why this fits you:**  \nAs someone who values art and detail, careful aftercare ensures your tattoo\u2019s color and lines stay crisp\u2014especially important for your sealion design",
          "citations": {
