          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "can occur. Patch testing is essential before tattooing. What should I know about choosing tattoo inks?",
          "user_rubrik": "What learning resources are available about tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 1,
          "text": "To choose safe, high-quality tattoo inks as a beginner in Germany, focus on these essentials:\n\n**1. Only Use Professional, Sterile Tattoo Inks**\n- Never use art, printer, or homemade inks\u2014these can contain unsafe chemicals or contaminants (clueweb22-en0038-45-11573).\n- Choose inks from reputable brands that are sterilized (gamma-irradiated) and comply with EU or US safety standards (clueweb22-en0040-42-02573, clueweb22-en0036-32-06054, clueweb22-en0008-17-01908).\n\n**2. Check Ingredients and Avoid High-Risk Pigments**\n- Black inks: Prefer carbon-based or logwood pigments; avoid those with benzo(a)pyrene (potential carcinogen) (clueweb22-en0027-92-14494, clueweb22-en0022-00-19271).\n- Reds: Avoid cadmium, mercury, iron oxide, and cinnabar\u2014these are linked to allergic reactions (clueweb22-en",
          "citations": {
