          "text": "In Germany, the safety of tattoo inks is regulated by the European Union's Tattoo REACH regulation, which restricts the use of certain chemicals in tattoo inks. When choosing ink, look for products that comply with this regulation. Some tattoo inks may contain hazardous substances that can cause skin allergies, genetic mutations, or cancer. Opt for reputable brands that provide information on the composition of their inks and ensure they meet the EU's safety standards. Be aware that around two-thirds fewer colors may be permitted due to the new regulations, so it's essential to check the ingredients and compliance of the ink before making a purchase. Always prioritize your safety and the safety of your clients when selecting tattoo inks.",
