      {
        "turn": 9,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! Do you know what \"REACH compliant\" means for tattoo needles? I see that label a lot here.",
          "user_rubrik": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "REACH compliant refers to the European Union's Registration, Evaluation, Authorization, and Restriction of Chemicals regulation. For tattoo needles, being REACH compliant means that the materials used in the needles, such as the metal and coatings, meet the EU's safety standards for chemical substances. This ensures that the needles are safe for use on human skin and do not contain any hazardous chemicals. Many tattoo needle manufacturers in Germany and other EU countries must comply with REACH regulations, which is why you may see this label on their products. It's a good sign that the needles have been tested and meet certain safety standards.",
