  {
    "runtag": "orga-no-no-no-llama70b",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "8-2",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m curious about tattooing 101. What\u2019s the best way to get started if I want to try tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Yes, a sedentary lifestyle can contribute to fatigue. Prolonged sitting can lead to decreased energy",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Not quite what I was looking for. Could you tell me specifically how one can start tattooing as a hobby? Maybe things I need or steps to follow?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "When considering a new tattoo, think about the design, placement, and size. Ensure the design resonates with you and has personal significance. Choose a placement that you're comfortable with,",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I already have a tattoo and know how to pick designs! I want to know how to actually start tattooing myself, as a hobby. What equipment do I need? Any beginner tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To start tattooing as a hobby, you'll need a tattoo machine, needles, ink, and practice skin. Begin with a beginner's kit and follow online tutorials. Ensure you follow proper hygiene and safety guidelines. Start by practicing on fake skin before moving to actual tattoos. It's also recommended to take a course or work under an experienced artist to learn proper techniques. Always prioritize sanitation and safety.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That sounds like a lot! Is there a specific type or brand of tattoo machine recommended for beginners? Also, what kind of fake skin do people usually use to practice?",
          "user_rubrik": "What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "For beginners, a rotary tattoo machine is recommended as it's easier to handle and more versatile. Brands like Cheyenne or FK Irons are popular among tattoo artists. For practice, you can use synthetic skin or pig skin, which can be found online or at tattoo supply stores. These materials mimic the feel and texture of human skin, allowing you to practice and hone your skills before working on actual tattoos. Always ensure you follow proper hygiene and safety guidelines when practicing.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, thanks! Is it okay to use any type of ink when practicing on fake skin, or should I get \u201creal\u201d tattoo ink right away? Also, do you know if it\u2019s legal to tattoo at home in Germany?",
          "user_rubrik": "What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "For practicing on fake skin, you can use tattoo ink, but it's not necessary. Some artists use alternative inks or even water to practice needle control and technique. However, if you plan to tattoo yourself or others, it's best to use real tattoo ink. In Germany, tattooing at home is legal, but it's recommended to follow proper hygiene and safety guidelines to avoid health risks. It's also important to note that some states in Germany may have specific regulations, so it's a good idea to check local laws and regulations. Always prioritize sanitation and safety.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Super useful! I\u2019ll stick to actual tattoo ink if I ever try it on real skin. Can you explain more about hygiene\u2014like what\u2019s absolutely necessary to keep my space and equipment safe for tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik": "What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "To maintain hygiene and safety, ensure your workspace is clean and well-ventilated. Use disposable needles and gloves, and sterilize your equipment regularly. Wash your hands thoroughly before and after tattooing. Use a tattoo machine with a removable and autoclavable parts. Keep ink caps and needles in a clean, dry place. Follow proper protocols for disposing of used needles and ink. Consider taking a bloodborne pathogens course to learn more about safety procedures. Always prioritize sanitation to prevent infections and ensure a safe tattooing experience. Regularly clean and disinfect your equipment and workspace to prevent cross-contamination.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
