          "text": "To maintain hygiene and safety, ensure your workspace is clean and well-ventilated. Use disposable needles and gloves, and sterilize your equipment regularly. Wash your hands thoroughly before and after tattooing. Use a tattoo machine with a removable and autoclavable parts. Keep ink caps and needles in a clean, dry place. Follow proper protocols for disposing of used needles and ink. Consider taking a bloodborne pathogens course to learn more about safety procedures. Always prioritize sanitation to prevent infections and ensure a safe tattooing experience. Regularly clean and disinfect your equipment and workspace to prevent cross-contamination.",
