          "user_utterance": "Interesting. I keep hearing about \"REACH compliant\" tattoo needles. What does that mean?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "REACH compliant tattoo needles refer to needles that meet the requirements of the Registration, Evaluation, Authorisation, and Restriction of Chemicals (REACH) regulation in the European Union. This regulation aims to ensure the safe use of chemicals in products, including tattoo needles. REACH compliant needles are made from materials that are free from certain hazardous substances, such as lead, mercury, and cadmium. These needles are designed to be safer for both the tattoo artist and the client. In Germany, where you live, REACH compliance is mandatory for tattoo needles, so it's essential to look for this certification when purchasing needles. This ensures that you're getting high-quality, safe needles for your tattooing hobby.  You can check the packaging or the manufacturer's website to confirm if the needles are REACH compliant.  It's also a good idea to consult with a professional tattoo artist or a tattoo supply expert to ensure you're getting the right needles for your specific needs.  Remember to always follow",
