        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Different types of tattoo needles exist, each designed for specific purposes. Round Liner (RL) needles are ideal for outlining designs. Round Shader (RS) needles are used for shading or coloring. Magnum needles, including Stacked Magnum (M1) for blending and shading smaller areas and Round Magnum (RM) for larger areas or sensitive skin, are also common. Flat (F) needles are recommended for shapes, intricate shading, or thin strokes. Other types like Double Magnum (M2) and Turbo needles also exist.",
