      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Alright, that makes sense. I see the term \u201cREACH compliant\u201d sometimes. What does that mean for tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "\"REACH compliant\" refers to the Registration, Evaluation, Authorization and Restriction of Chemicals, an EU regulation. For tattooing, it primarily regulates the chemical composition of tattoo inks, restricting or banning substances linked to health risks like allergies or cancer. The provided information does not specify \"REACH compliant\" requirements for the physical tattoo needles themselves, but rather for the inks used with them.",
