        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it, thanks for clarifying! Are there any learning resources on regulations for tattooing in Germany?",
          "user_rubrik": "What learning resources are available about tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "In Germany, tattooing is regulated by the EU's REACH for inks, banning certain chemicals. German law also governs ink composition, making some pigments illegal, and considers tattooing a voluntary assault. Studio hygiene, sterilization, and age restrictions are also in place. For learning resources, consult the \"Legal status of tattooing in European countries\" Wikipedia article. Additionally, the German Federal Institute for Risk Assessment (BfR) is a key source for tattoo ink safety information.",
