        "turn": 10,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yes, apprenticeships sound good! How do you usually approach a tattoo shop about that?",
          "user_rubrik": "What learning resources are available about tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "To approach tattoo shops for an apprenticeship, start by researching reputable shops in Berlin with artists whose work you admire. Get tattooed there and spend time building relationships with the artists to demonstrate your genuine interest. Simultaneously, develop a strong portfolio of your drawings, focusing on tattoo designs. Once you have a solid portfolio and a connection, talk to the artists directly about your interest and present your work. Be prepared for tough competition and potential rejections, as this process can take time.",
