      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that's better\u2014so it applies to inks, not to needles themselves, right? Are there tattoo machines or equipment that need to be REACH compliant too?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "While REACH compliance primarily focuses on the chemical composition of tattoo inks, it also applies to the chemical substances used in the manufacturing of tattoo machines and other equipment. This means that materials, solvents, or paints used to produce these items must comply with REACH regulations if they contain restricted substances or are imported/manufactured in specific quantities within the EU.",
