  {
    "runtag": "uva-gpt5-bm25-debertav3-gpt5",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "8-2",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Oh, I\u2019m actually here to learn more about tattooing for beginners. What\u2019s a good way to get started if you want to try tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to start tattooing as a hobby?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great hobby, but treat it like a craft with real safety rules. a simple path to start : - build fundamentals : draw flash sheets daily. practice clean lines, shading, stippling. - learn hygiene first : take a blood \u2011 borne pathogens / hygiene course ( hygieneschulung ). use nitrile gloves, barrier film, clip \u2011 cord / machine covers, surface disinfectant, and a sharps container. - gear for practice : a beginner rotary pen with cartridge needles, small power supply or wireless battery, foot switch optional. get quality silicone practice skins, stencil paper, green soap, and a petroleum \u2011 free glide. use reach \u2011 compliant inks ( required in germany ). - practice only on fake skin or fruit at first. do dozens of line, whip, and packing drills. adjust voltage / hand speed ; keep needle hang short ( about 1 \u2013 2 mm ) ; stretch skin lightly. - legal in germany : no minors ; reach inks ; don \u2019 t tattoo people for money without meeting local gesundheitsamt hygiene requirements. - level up : seek an apprenticeship or short workshop and studio shadowing. - disposal : put used cartridges / needles in a sharp",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0013-41-04803:0": 0.7764055132865906,
            "clueweb22-en0007-03-16021:0": -0.5237298607826233,
            "clueweb22-en0046-37-06350:4": -0.8070953488349915,
            "clueweb22-en0017-03-07180:0": -1.0199668407440186,
            "clueweb22-en0024-93-15844:1": -1.3585478067398071
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Ah thanks, super helpful! So, about the equipment\u2014what kind of rotary pen and cartridge needles would you recommend for a beginner? I\u2019ve seen lots of kits online, but I\u2019m not sure if they\u2019re good.",
          "user_rubrik": "What equipments are needed to start tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great question. keep it simple, reliable, and safe. rotary pen ( beginner - friendly ) - budget : dragonhawk atom or wormhole tk108 pen kits. use the pen and power, skip the bundled inks. - mid : dragonhawk mast tour or m4 ( light, consistent, 3. 5 \u2013 4. 0 mm stroke ). - if budget allows : cheyenne hawk pen / sol nova ( german brand, very reliable ). what to look for - stroke around 3. 5 \u2013 4. 0 mm for all \u2011 round lining / shading. - universal rca connection. - start wired ( a small power supply is steadier than a battery ). cartridge needles ( must be membrane - sealed ) - budget : wjx / mast pro, ez v \u2011 select. - mid / pro : kwadron optima, cheyenne safety cartridges. starter sizes ( all # 12 = 0. 35 mm ) - liners : 1205rl, 1207rl, 1209rl. - shader : 1207rs. - mags : 1207m1 or 1209m1 ( start small ). also grab - decent rca cable, small psu ( e. g., critical",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0013-41-04803:0": 0.9079364538192749,
            "clueweb22-en0027-86-19967:0": 0.3819809854030609,
            "clueweb22-en0021-73-10825:0": 0.1296359896659851,
            "clueweb22-en0023-17-07995:0": -0.18203893303871155,
            "clueweb22-en0007-03-16021:0": -0.5580921769142151
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Cool, thanks, that clears up a lot! Can you explain the types of tattoo needles and what they\u2019re for? I keep seeing codes like RL, RS, M1 on needle packs\u2014what do they actually mean?",
          "user_rubrik": "What different tattoo needle types exist?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "here \u2019 s how to read those codes and what they \u2019 re for : how to read a code ( example : 1207rl ) - 12 = needle diameter / gauge ( # 12 = 0. 35 mm ; # 10 \u201c bugpin \u201d = 0. 30 mm ; # 8 = 0. 25 mm ) - 07 = needle count in the grouping - rl = grouping / type common types - rl ( round liner ) : needles grouped tight in a circle. for crisp lines and fine details. sizes 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 14 change line weight. - rs ( round shader ) : looser circle. for small fills, soft shading, pepper shading, and packing tight areas without line \u201c cut. \u201d - f or flat : single straight row. can be used for lining or geometric work ; less common than mags in cartridges. - m1 ( weaved magnum ) : two staggered rows. workhorse for color packing and shading larger areas. - m2 ( double stack magnum ) : denser than m1 ; faster saturation, more trauma \u2014 use with care. - rm / cm ( curved / round magnum ) : magnum with a slight arc ; softer edges, smooth blends, great",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0013-41-04803:0": 0.7730734348297119,
            "clueweb22-en0031-20-16817:0": 0.6925761699676514,
            "clueweb22-en0027-86-19967:0": 0.4291338324546814,
            "clueweb22-en0022-58-06316:0": 0.33193904161453247,
            "clueweb22-en0009-13-08595:0": 0.3012893497943878
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes so much sense now, thanks! Are there any specific places in Germany\u2014maybe online shops\u2014where beginners can buy these tattoo needles and practice kits safely and legally?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where to buy tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "yes \u2014 here are reputable eu / german retailers that ship fast within germany and stock compliant gear : - barber dts ( barberdts. com / de ) : cheyenne / kwadron cartridges, machines, practice skins, hygiene, sharps containers. - killer ink tattoo ( killerinktattoo. de ) : wide selection ; a pound of flesh practice skins ; cheyenne, kwadron, ez, membranes. - cheyenne ( cheyennetattoo. com ) : german brand ; hawk / sol nova machines and safety cartridges ; reach - compliant. - tattooland de ( tattooland. com / de ) : ships from nl ; ez v - select, kwadron, panthera inks ( reach 2022 ), barrier supplies. - painful pleasures eu ( painfulpleasures. eu ) : eu warehouse ; cartridges, grips, practice skins, disposables. - amazon. de : fine for budget pens and practice skins ; avoid kit inks unless clearly reach / eu - safe. what to look for : - cartridge needles : membrane - sealed ( cheyenne safety, kwadron optima, ez v - select, mast pro ). - inks ( reach 2022 + ) : world",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0013-41-04803:0": 0.7374837398529053,
            "clueweb22-en0046-33-06459:0": 0.35937607288360596,
            "clueweb22-en0027-86-19967:0": 0.3041021227836609,
            "clueweb22-en0004-09-01120:0": 0.09327295422554016,
            "clueweb22-en0021-73-10825:0": 0.045881591737270355
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Super useful! You mentioned \"REACH-compliant\"\u2014what exactly does that mean for tattoo needles? Is it just about ink, or do the needles themselves need to meet some kind of REACH standards too?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is REACH compliant in tattoo needles?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "short answer : reach mainly matters for inks, not needles. - what reach is : it \u2019 s the eu chemicals law. since jan 2022, a reach restriction limits thousands of substances in tattoo and pmu inks and sets labeling rules. \u201c reach \u2011 compliant ink \u201d means it meets those annex xvii limits. - needles / cartridges : these are \u201c articles, \u201d not chemical mixtures. they aren \u2019 t covered by the tattoo \u2011 ink restriction. they still fall under general reach duties ( e. g., suppliers must avoid restricted substances and disclose any svhcs > 0. 1 % ), but there \u2019 s no special \u201c reach standard \u201d you as a buyer need to check for needles. what to look for in needles / cartridges instead : - 316l surgical stainless steel needles ; medical \u2011 grade plastic housings - internal membrane to prevent backflow - eo \u2011 sterilized, single \u2011 use blisters with sterilization indicator, lot / batch number, and expiry date - manufacturer quality marks ( e. g., iso 13485 / iso 9001 ) and clear eu supplier info bottom line : verify reach compliance for inks ; for needles, prioritize sterile, membrane \u2011 sealed,",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0013-41-04803:0": 0.8268405199050903,
            "clueweb22-en0022-58-06316:0": 0.2791859805583954,
            "clueweb22-en0027-86-19967:0": 0.26003724336624146,
            "clueweb22-en0004-09-01120:0": 0.1112794429063797,
            "clueweb22-en0021-73-10825:0": 0.047273360192775726
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it, that clears it up! What about online learning\u2014are there good YouTube channels or online courses for learning tattoo basics and hygiene? I\u2019m more into watching stuff than reading big manuals.",
          "user_rubrik": "What learning resources are available about tattooing?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great idea. video - first options i recommend : youtube - electric linda : clear basics on setup, station hygiene, wrapping, aftercare. - tattooing 101 : beginner - friendly drills, needle / setup explainers, cross \u2011 contamination dos / don \u2019 ts. - cheyenne professional tattoo equipment : german brand ; de / en webinars on hygiene, machine setup, cartridge safety. - killer ink tattoo : demos on machine setup, needle types, wrapping a station, cleaning. - barber dts : gear guides plus sterilization, barrier use, sharps handling. - fk irons : solid hygiene and machine handling fundamentals ( even if you don \u2019 t use their gear ). structured online courses - bloodborne pathogens for body art ( body art training group, apt, protrainings eu ) : video - based, with certificate. - look for \u201c hygieneschulung tatowierer online \u201d or \u201c infektionsschutz / hygiene schulung \u201d accepted by your local gesundheitsamt ; many providers offer video modules + certificate. tip : watch a hygiene playlist, then practice a full sterile setup / teardown on your desk : wrap surfaces, machine / cords, bottle bags, glove",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0024-24-00009:6": -2.558283805847168,
            "clueweb22-en0024-24-00009:5": -3.6375603675842285,
